    heroSubhead: "Brief solution-focused therapy is a goal-oriented, strengths-based approach that helps people move forward on specific problems such as stress, low mood, worry, and life transitions. At Blue Willow Psychiatry, we focus on what you want to change and the resources you already have.",
    heroImage: {"src":"/images/stock/brief-solution-focused-therapy.jpg","alt":"From above of blurred unrecognizable female psychologist sitting in office near table with clipboard and pen during session in office","width":1200,"height":627},
    introHeading: "What is Brief Solution-Focused Therapy?",
    intro: ["Brief solution-focused therapy, often shortened to SFBT, is a form of talk therapy that concentrates on the present and future rather than lengthy analysis of the past. Instead of asking only why a problem began, the therapist helps you describe what life would look like when things improve, and what small steps could lead there.","The approach rests on a few simple ideas: change is always happening, problems are not constant, and people have strengths and past successes they can build on. Techniques include defining clear goals, exploring exceptions (times when the problem was smaller or absent), scaling questions that help you rate progress, and identifying the next small step.","SFBT has been studied for a range of concerns, including stress, adjustment difficulties, and relationship and school or work problems, and research suggests it can be a useful short-term option for many people. It may be especially appealing if you want a practical, focused experience. It is not the right fit for every situation, and we will discuss alternatives or combined treatment when appropriate."],
    signsHeading: "Signs this approach may be a good fit",
    signsList: ["Feeling stuck on a specific problem and wanting practical next steps","Stress, worry, or low mood that is affecting work, school, or relationships","A major life transition such as a move, job change, or loss","Difficulty making a decision or following through on goals","Conflict patterns at home or work you want to change","A preference for a focused, short-term style of therapy"],
    bullets: ["Goal-oriented, strengths-based sessions focused on what you want to change","Techniques such as the miracle question, scaling questions, and exception-finding","Collaborative, respectful sessions centered on your priorities","Short-term focus that aims to wrap up once your goals are met","Option to consider medication or other therapy alongside, as a psychiatry practice"],
    approachHeading: "Our Approach to Brief Solution-Focused Therapy",
    approach: [{"title":"Initial Assessment","body":"We begin by listening. You describe what brings you in, what has been difficult, and just as importantly, what is already working. We discuss your history and clarify what you would like to be different.","iconPath":"M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z"},{"title":"Personalized Plan","body":"Together we set clear, realistic goals in your own words. We outline how sessions will focus on those goals and how we will recognize progress, so therapy stays purposeful.","iconPath":"M9 20l-5.447-2.724A1 1 0 013 16.382V5.618a1 1 0 011.447-.894L9 7m0 13l6-3m-6 3V7m6 10l4.553 2.276A1 1 0 0021 18.382V7.618a1 1 0 00-.553-.894L15 4m0 13V4m0 0L9 7"},{"title":"Ongoing Support","body":"Each session builds on small steps you have already taken. We review progress, adjust goals as life changes, and decide together when you have what you need and when additional support may help.","iconPath":"M4.318 6.318a4.5 4.5 0 000 6.364L12 20.364l7.682-7.682a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364-6.364L12 7.636l-1.318-1.318a4.5 4.5 0 00-6.364 0z"}],
    benefits: [{"title":"Strengths-Based","body":"We focus on what you want to change and the resources you already have."},{"title":"Practical and Focused","body":"Sessions concentrate on small, concrete changes and clear next steps."},{"title":"Short-Term by Design","body":"Because the approach is brief, the aim is to wrap up once your goals are met, with a plan for keeping progress going."},{"title":"Integrated Psychiatric Perspective","body":"Therapy can be considered alongside a broader view of your mental health, including medication when appropriate."}],
    timelineHeading: "What to Expect",
    timeline: [{"title":"First Visit","body":"We talk through your concerns, strengths, and hopes, and begin shaping the goals you want to work toward."},{"title":"Week 2-4","body":"Sessions focus on small, concrete changes. Many people begin noticing moments when the problem is less intense."},{"title":"Month 1-3","body":"You build on what is working, refine your goals, and practice new approaches in daily life."},{"title":"Long-term","body":"Because the approach is brief, the aim is to wrap up once your goals are met, with a plan for keeping progress going."}],
    extraSections: [{"heading":"What to Expect in Sessions","body":["In sessions, you can expect techniques such as the \"miracle question,\" which invites you to imagine your life after the problem is resolved, along with scaling questions, exception-finding, and goal setting. Sessions are collaborative, respectful, and centered on your priorities.","Because we are a psychiatry practice, therapy can be considered alongside a broader view of your mental health. If symptoms suggest that other treatment, such as medication or another therapy type, might help, we will discuss those options with you."]},{"heading":"Timeline Note","body":["Every person's experience is different, and progress is not always a straight line."]}],
    faqs: [{"q":"How many sessions does brief solution-focused therapy take?","a":"It is designed to be short-term, and the number of sessions varies by person and goal. Some people find a handful of sessions is enough, while others benefit from more. We review progress regularly and decide together."},{"q":"How is it different from traditional talk therapy?","a":"Traditional approaches often explore the origins of a problem in depth. Solution-focused therapy spends more time on what you want your life to look like, times when things go better, and the strengths you already have."},{"q":"Is it appropriate for every concern?","a":"It can be helpful for many everyday and situational challenges. Some conditions need a different or broader treatment plan, and we will talk openly with you about what fits your needs."},{"q":"Can it be combined with medication?","a":"Yes. Therapy and medication are often used together, and as a psychiatry practice we can discuss whether medication is a reasonable part of your care. Any decision is made together with you."},{"q":"How do I get started?","a":"Call us at (435) 200-3430 or use our contact page. You can also visit us at 1102 W 60 S, Ste 6, Tooele, Utah 84074."}],
