    heroSubhead: "Cognitive behavioral therapy, or CBT, is a structured, practical approach that helps you see how thoughts, feelings and actions affect one another, and learn skills to change the patterns that keep you stuck. At Blue Willow Psychiatry, CBT can be part of a plan built around your goals.",
    heroImage: {"src": "/images/stock/cognitive-behavioral-therapy.jpg", "alt": "A therapist writing notes in a notebook during a session while a client sits on a green sofa in the background.", "width": 1200, "height": 627},
    introHeading: "What Is Cognitive Behavioral Therapy?",
    intro: ["Cognitive behavioral therapy is a form of talk therapy built on a simple idea: the way we think about a situation shapes how we feel and what we do. When thoughts become overly negative, rigid or fearful, they can feed anxiety, low mood and habits that make life harder. CBT helps you notice those patterns and test new ways of thinking and responding.", "The work is collaborative and focused on the present. Together we identify specific problems and goals, then build skills such as recognizing and reframing unhelpful thoughts, gradually facing situations you have been avoiding, problem solving, and building routines that support your mood. Practice between visits is a key part of the approach, so the skills carry into daily life.", "CBT is one of the most widely studied forms of psychotherapy. Research supports it for depression, anxiety disorders, panic, insomnia and many other concerns, and it is often used alongside medication. It is not the right fit for every person or every problem, and we will talk openly about what fits your needs."],
    signsHeading: "Signs CBT may be a good fit",
